00:59:28,695 --> 00:59:34,695
Jack the Giant Slayer (previously titled Jack the Giant Killer) is a 2013 American fantasy adventure film directed by Bryan
Singer and written by Darren Lemke, Christopher McQuarrie and Dan Studney, from a story by Lemke and David Dobkin.

13
01:04:26,086 --> 01:04:32,086
The film, based on the British fairy tales "Jack the Giant Killer" and "Jack and the Beanstalk", stars
Nicholas Hoult, Eleanor Tomlinson, Stanley Tucci, Ian McShane, Bill Nighy, and Ewan McGregor.

14
01:09:23,478 --> 01:09:29,478
The film tells the story of Jack, a young farmhand who must save a captured princess from a race of giants after
accidentally opening a gateway to their land in the sky while also contending with a crooked lord.

15
01:14:20,869 --> 01:14:26,869
Development of Jack the Giant Slayer began in 2005,
when Lemke first pitched the idea.

16
01:19:18,260 --> 01:19:24,260
Caruso was hired to direct the film in January 2009, but in September of that year, Caruso
was replaced by Singer, who hired McQuarrie and Studney to rework the script.

17
01:24:15,652 --> 01:24:21,652
The main characters were cast between February and March 2011, and principal photography began in
April 2011 in England with locations in Somerset, Gloucestershire and Norfolk.

18
01:29:13,043 --> 01:29:19,043
The release of the film was moved back in post-production to
allow more time for visual effects and marketing.

19
01:34:10,434 --> 01:34:16,434
Jack the Giant Slayer premiered on February 26, 2013, in Hollywood.

20
01:39:07,826 --> 01:39:13,826
It was released theatrically in the United States on March 1, 2013, receiving mixed reviews from critics and
was a box-office failure, earning $197 million worldwide against a budget of $185–200 million.

21
01:44:05,217 --> 01:44:11,217
The film explores themes of nostalgic, based on fairy tale, giant.

22
